+
+### Replacing artwork after metadata or review edits
+
+Prepared artwork and its retained source original have independent immutable revision numbers. Editing geometry or recording review evidence creates a new prepared revision without inventing a source revision. A later upload or prepared sprite starts or advances its own original-source history and references that exact original. Earlier artwork, source bytes and review records remain available through history, Save/Reload and bundle transfer. No migration or renumbering is required.
+
+Maintenance prompt: “Upload and stage an asset, edit its metadata, record review evidence, then upload and stage another image. Also review an asset before its first upload and prepare two successive sprite edits. Check each exact asset ID advances independently, pending preparation cannot be replaced accidentally, and the prepared asset references the correct source revision. Save/reload and export/import every original byte and earlier record. Distinguish modeled handler checks from native picker, pixel decoding, actual downloads and public-release evidence.”
