+# P04 — independent original-source revisions
+
+Status: qualified source candidate; release acceptance remains pending.
+
+Base: `8cffb36b29a38013eb9213845efd675c4864c9d8`.
+
+A metadata edit or review appends a prepared-asset revision without a new source original. The upload path reused that prepared revision number for its different original-source asset ID. The next image or sprite could therefore fail with “New assets revision must be the next revision.” Original bytes remained intact, but ordinary iterative authoring could not continue.
+
+The fix allocates the original's next revision from that exact source ID. It retains immutable history, source/derivative parent references, validation limits and storage formats. No data migration or skipped-revision exception is introduced.
+
+## Verification
+
+- Baseline actual-host regression reproduces the precise rejection after metadata editing.
+- Final six complete test files pass 45/45 on Node 20.19.5 and 22.22.2, with no skips or failures: presentation Studio, transfer history, slot history, sprite editor, actual host loading, and published Studio.
+- Mounted-host sequences exercise upload → metadata → upload, review → upload, two sprite preparations, refusal of duplicate pending preparation, and review before the first original upload. Each source and derivative advances independently.
+- Save and Reload retain the selected revisions; every earlier immutable asset record and byte remains exact. The resulting document and all files also pass binary bundle export/import with the final derivative pointing to source revision 5.
+- An independent read-only review found no blocking correctness issue.
+- A separate baseline compiled-collection check exports 1,351 asset records and 133 files into a 7,399,336-byte bundle, SHA-256 `dd8d17b2227fef4d2e6b63a3f73253be1dbf4f870a4f74325fff24f7ce2371e3`. Node 22 import preserves document/payload bytes; Node 20 import/re-export produces identical bytes.
+
+The tests use modeled DOM, storage and predetermined valid PNG encoding. Transfer verification checks headers/hashes with `decodeImage: null`. These are not claims of native picker operation, pixel fidelity, physical input or public deployment.
+
+The attempted native transfer trial remained incomplete: both fresh Studio origins loaded normally, but browser-control activation failed to operate even native disclosures, and filechooser observation timed out. No product input defect is inferred. There was no browser upload, saved revision, actual download or fresh-origin import in that trial. Native transfer remains an acceptance item.
+
+Reproduce with the six complete source test files above. The isolated review packet retains baseline failure, both runtime TAP logs, exact loaded-source receipts and independent compiled transfer outputs under `.cache/p04-studio-source-revisions-8cff-r1/` and `.cache/p17-studio-transfer-8cff-r1/`. Do not add those locally generated theme archives to a public release as approved artwork.
+
+The release owner must integrate related hunks, synchronize the next unused version, run all six release gates and applicable build/browser checks against the exact commit, then freeze, deploy and verify public behavior. This source qualification does not waive those gates.
